            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery spasm as a cause of chest pain and re-elevation of ST segment and cardiogenic shock after PTCA.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>188-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case that underwent successful percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty in cardiogenic shock but after half an hour, again had severe chest pain with re-elevation of ST segment and was found to have coronary artery spasm as a cause of recurrence of symptoms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
